+# Run B report
+
+Generated only `04-rubble.png`, `05-ajar.png`, and `06-open.png` using the built-in image generation tool, each as an independent edit of `../ref/wall-template.png`, with `transparent_background: true`. Exactly one generation per image; no retries. Run A was not performed.
+
+Saved all three PNGs under their exact requested names. SHA-256 comparisons confirm the saved files are byte-for-byte identical to the tool outputs. No pixel changes, resizing, cropping, background removal, matting, or alpha repair were applied. The input template was not changed.
+
+Results: rubble shows broken wood, bent bands and three stumps; ajar shows a gap at the left post and a foreshortened three-stake leaf; open shows a clear passage with the leaf overlapping behind the right post. All retain the painted wood/iron style.
+
+Validation and deviations: all three outputs are 1254x1254, not the requested 1024x1024, despite explicit prompt instructions. Each has an alpha channel ranging from 0 to 255. Exact original scale, pixel registration, and y=940 baseline are therefore not met. Visual review also shows the rubble is taller than the intended one-third height. Nonzero-alpha bounds extend beyond the main visible objects, so alpha cleanliness is not certified. These are unmodified first-generation results, not fully compliant production frames. The brief prohibits correction or regeneration, so the deviations were retained and reported.
+
+## Exact prompts
+
+All calls used the original template as the sole referenced image and enabled transparent_background.
+
+### 04
+
+Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit the supplied approved wall template into one game animation frame. Output exactly 1024x1024 with genuine transparent background, preserving generated alpha. Match template painted soft shading, dark outlines, warm wood and grey iron, top-left light and three-quarter high camera. Original wall has FIVE pointed stakes, left/back tallest to right/front lowest, two rails and iron bands with square rivets. Preserve original canvas, scale and placement, never rescale, recenter or crop. Baseline y=940. Only wood and iron; no ground, ground patch, ground shadow, dust, smoke, glow, motion lines, sparks, text, border or backdrop.  Frame 04-rubble.png: wall fallen into a low heap of broken stakes, snapped rails and bent iron bands lying flat. Center heap where original wall stood, resting at y=940. Maximum heap height about 240px (one third original wall), no wider than 1.25 times original wall width (~830px). Leave the upper canvas empty transparent. Two or three SHORT broken stake stumps still stand at original feet. Do not retain any tall upright stakes. No dust or ground patch.
+
+### 05
+
+Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit the supplied approved wall template into one game animation frame. Output exactly 1024x1024 with genuine transparent background, preserving generated alpha. Match template painted soft shading, dark outlines, warm wood and grey iron, top-left light and three-quarter high camera. Original wall has FIVE pointed stakes, left/back tallest to right/front lowest, two rails and iron bands with square rivets. Preserve original canvas, scale and placement, never rescale, recenter or crop. Baseline y=940. Only wood and iron; no ground, ground patch, ground shadow, dust, smoke, glow, motion lines, sparks, text, border or backdrop.  Frame 05-ajar.png: convert same wall to half-open gate. FIRST stake at viewer-left and FIFTH stake viewer-right are fixed posts: preserve exactly their template size, shape, bands, tips and pixel positions (left post approx x180..328,y216..760; right post x700..846,y325..940). The middle THREE stakes, with their own short rail pieces and iron bands, form ONE leaf hinged at the FIFTH/rightmost stake. Rotate only that leaf about 45 degrees BACKWARD away from viewer, foreshortened narrower and angled into depth BEHIND the fifth stake. Same physical heights and appearance as originals. A clear transparent gap opens beside the FIRST/left stake. No rails crossing that empty gap. Keep both fixed posts exactly registered to reference. Render only a single half-open leaf with exactly three stakes, plus two fixed posts.
+
+### 06
+
+Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit the supplied approved wall template into one game animation frame. Output exactly 1024x1024 with genuine transparent background, preserving generated alpha. Match template painted soft shading, dark outlines, warm wood and grey iron, top-left light and three-quarter high camera. Original wall has FIVE pointed stakes, left/back tallest to right/front lowest, two rails and iron bands with square rivets. Preserve original canvas, scale and placement, never rescale, recenter or crop. Baseline y=940. Only wood and iron; no ground, ground patch, ground shadow, dust, smoke, glow, motion lines, sparks, text, border or backdrop.  Frame 06-open.png: fully open gate. FIRST stake viewer-left and FIFTH stake viewer-right stay EXACTLY where and how they are in template, unchanged fixed gateposts. Their original approximate extents in 1024 canvas: left x180..328 y216..760; right x700..846 y325..940. Middle THREE stakes and their short rails and iron bands form a single leaf hinged at FIFTH/rightmost post. Leaf swung fully BACKWARD away from viewer about 90 degrees; seen almost EDGE-ON as a VERY NARROW column of three stakes overlapping behind fifth post, receding into depth. Same physical stake heights and appearance. Passage between first and fifth posts is COMPLETELY OPEN TRANSPARENT, with NO stakes or rails in the passage. All rails go with leaf. Preserve post positions and exact scale; no reframing. Total five stakes, three heavily occluded in narrow edge-on leaf behind right post. Output 1024x1024.
+

